# Learning Python (bonus, 9 days)

The next teaching block is **beginner Python for machine learning**. It lasts **9 days**. It is a **bonus chapter**, like NumPy and Pandas. It does **not** count as Days 13 to 21 of the 100 day series.

Wait for the user's notes. Do not invent a Python syllabus.

## Site order (strict)

Teaching order on the site and in the sidebar:

1. Day 12 Anaconda Setup (`days/day12.html`)
2. **Learning Python** (`days/python1.html` … `days/python9.html`)
3. Learning NumPy (`days/numpy.html`)
4. Learning Pandas (`days/pandas.html`)
5. Day 13 onward

Never put Python after NumPy, after Day 38, or as `days/day39.html`.

## Files

One file per Python day:

```
days/python1.html
days/python2.html
...
days/python9.html
```

Each file is only that day's `chapter-divider` plus `lesson-card` blocks.

```html
<div class="chapter-divider reveal" id="chapter-python-1" data-chapter="python-1">
  <span class="chapter-divider__pill">Python 1</span>
  <h2 class="chapter-divider__title">Title from the user's notes</h2>
  <p class="chapter-divider__note">Short description. This bonus day does not count as a course day.</p>
</div>

<article class="lesson-card reveal" id="section-N" data-section="N" data-chapter="python-1">
  ...
</article>
```

Use `data-chapter="python-1"` through `python-9`. Pill text is `Python 1` … `Python 9`, never `Day 1`.

## Wire into index.html

TOC: after the Day 12 block, before the NumPy block. Nine `.toc-chapter` entries (`data-chapter="python-1"` … `python-9`).

Includes, in this order:

```html
<div data-include='days/day12.html'></div>
<div data-include='days/python1.html'></div>
<!-- python2 … python9 -->
<div data-include='days/numpy.html'></div>
```

Hero and footer stay on the latest **numbered** 100 day (currently Day 38). Python does not change "Day N of 100 published".

## Lesson numbers

Follow `lesson-numbering.mdc`. Python sits after Day 12, so it continues from Day 12's last lesson, not from the latest published 100 day. Then NumPy, Pandas, and Day 13 onward shift up.

## CSS

Add `--chapter-python-1` … `--chapter-python-9` in `styles.css`, plus divider and card color rules. Then run `embed-css.sh`.

## Code lessons

Python days are code heavy. Use `.code-io` with input and output. Do not dump only a `pre` block. Follow `visual-teaching.mdc`.
